# Drafted by Gemini (R13 village_after), edited.

~ jeremiah_reward
Narrator: Jeremiah unfolds the crumpled paper with soil-stained thumbs, squinting down at William's shaky hand by lantern light.
jeremiah_stover [weary]: William writes that the crow is dead and the stalks are down. I never thought you would bring any of those poor folk back.
jeremiah_stover [neutral]: A bargain is a bargain on this moor. Here is fifty gold pieces for each of the four of you, two hundred in all.
gold +200
set foxwillow_paid
-> phillip_match

~ phillip_match
Narrator: Mr. Phillip snaps his pocketbook shut with a crisp click and tosses a velvet purse from palm to palm.
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: Well now, a Druskenvald cannot let an honest farmer outdo the estate in generosity, can he? It would be dreadful manners.
phillip_druskenvald [sly]: Take another two hundred from the family coffers, old sports. You earned every penny out there in the straw and smoke.
interject name:silas_vane: Count the coin twice when a toff smiles like that, friend, just in case.
gold +200
set phillip_matched_reward
-> adela_paintings

~ rain_recruits
Narrator: Sister Rain smells of wet wool and crushed marigolds, her bright hair catching the square's firelight as she gathers packs and spades.
sister_rain [smile]: Bless your mud-caked boots! The Patient Lady heard the song return to Foxwillow, and I have six strong hands ready to walk east with fresh seed.
sister_rain [angry]: Let the crows and the rot do their worst. We will turn that sour ash until green shoots break through again, I swear it.
set sister_rain_recruited
-> END

~ adela_paintings
Narrator: Lady Adela props two small canvases against the well stone, the oil paint still tacky and smelling of linseed and turpentine.
adela_druskenvald [neutral]: Little Gaston painted both of these in his sleep last night. First, a maze of dry corn beneath a golden harvest moon, which you have already settled.
adela_druskenvald [afraid]: Look at the second, darlings: a cloud of black bats boiling up before a moon the colour of fresh blood. Watch the sky on your next road.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Leathery wings, flying in a drove. I shall want a fresh page for those.
set adela_paintings_seen
-> END
